  "distractor_rules": {
    "roots": [
      "Offer exactly four not-contractions. Exactly one matches the two-word form in the stem.",
      "Never offer I'm, he's, she's, we're, they're, it's, I've, or that's.",
      "Always write contractions with an apostrophe: isn't, not isnt.",
      "Tier 1 wrong choices use distant helping verbs so the match is obvious.",
      "Tier 2 distractors come from nearby tense or number pairs such as don't, doesn't, and didn't.",
      "Tier 3 uses near-miss pairs: wasn't/weren't, won't/wouldn't, don't/doesn't, can't/couldn't.",
      "Keep stems as kid statements that hold the expanded form. Never put the answer contraction in the stem.",
      "Cover many not-pairs across the pool: is/are, do/does/did, was/were, will/would, can/could, should, has/have/had.",
      "One right answer only. Never write two contractions that both fit.",
      "Use <NAME> from names.txt. Never write a real name."
    ]
  },
